Chapter: EffectNonfinalAct
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A def declared pure (: Integer, no effect row) whose act block
 performs Console I/O in a NON-final statement, with a pure final
 statement. An earlier act-inference loop kept only the last
 statement's type, so the Console effect vanished before the
 def-boundary effect-subset check and declared-pure code could
 perform I/O. The act now carries the union of every statement's
 effects, so Console surfaces and CDX2031 rejects the undeclared
 effect.

Section: Definitions

  sneaky : Integer
  sneaky = act
    (print-line-uni "covert channel")
    42
  end

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show sneaky)
  end
